cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Markov-K-means: stopping K-means on its unstable tail and settling the last points from their label histories"
abstract: >-
  Markov-K-means watches the state of a K-means run (how many points still change cluster,
  whether the centers travel or only jitter, whether the clusters reorganise or only swap
  members), stops once only a few boundary points are still changing, and settles those
  points from their own label history: a point that moved and stayed keeps its new cluster,
  a point that keeps switching gets its share of time in each cluster as a soft membership.
  It works on exact Lloyd (Hamerly), 1/count mini-batch and constant-step (EMA) mini-batch
  K-means, and is a scikit-learn compatible estimator.
